  "releaseNotes": "Security fix: credential-bearing HTTP header values are now redacted in diagnostic output.\n\n      Previously caller-supplied header values were written verbatim in two places: one Debug line\n      per header as it was added to a request, and the Trace request and response dumps. Any\n      credential attached to a query was therefore retained for the life of the consumer log store.\n\n      Note the Debug path, which fires a level higher than the Trace dumps, so a consumer running at\n      Debug rather than Trace was still affected.\n\n      This client applies no credential of its own, so redaction matches a general set of header\n      names plus name fragments rather than a scheme this library controls. The authentication\n      scheme and the credential length are retained, so requests remain diagnosable.\n\n      Request rendering that forms part of the wire format, such as the batch payload built by\n      HttpMessageContent, is deliberately unchanged. Redacting there would corrupt the request.\n\n      Consumers should upgrade and then review existing Debug and Trace logs for previously\n      captured credentials.\n\n      Initial release with OData V4 support, query builder, CRUD operations, pagination, retry\n      logic, and logging.",
